{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Comedy of Errors"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Going Dutch"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le10ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Using the Structure<span class=\"italic\"> I wish  </span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use \u201c<span class=\"italic\">I wish</span> ...\u201d to talk about things you do not have or do, or you cannot have or do. </br>You use <span class=\"strong\">wish</span>, the past form of the verb or the past participle of the verb to talk about imaginary situation in the present or in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The verb<span class=\"italic\"> wish</span> introduces an idea. After <span class=\"italic\">wish</span>, you use a verb in the past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I wish I knew ... </br>I wish I had ...</br> I wish you were ..."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure:  </br>Wish + Simple Past tense"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I wish Sally was here.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would like Sally to be here, but she isn't going to be.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I wish that you lived close by.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would like you to live close by, but you don't.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wish I had some extra money with me."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wish ... that you lived close by, but you don't, sorry."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wish Sally was here, so she could say you were being a jerk."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wish you could come with us tonight."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Degrees of Necessity"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modals must and have (got) to to express necessities in the past or in the present. </br>You use the negative forms of the modals <span class=\"italic\">need to </span>and <span class=\"italic\">have to </span>to express absence of necessity in the past or in the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Must</span> refers to a necessary condition that comes from the subject and may be directed at the subject or the person the subject is talking to or about. It is used to express a strong necessity. <ul>Example: </br><span class=\"italic\"> I must set up this online profile by tomorrow. </br>An ideal date must include good food. </span></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have (got)  to</span> expresses external obligations, which come from outside of the subject. These may be rules and regulations over which the subject has no control. It is used to express necessity in a lower degree than with <span class=\"italic\">must. </span><ul>Example: </br><span class=\"italic\">My ideal date has to be tall, preferably.</span></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Absence of obligation is expressed with the <span class=\"strong\">negative form of have to</span>, not with mustn't. <ul>Example: </br><span class=\"italic\">My ideal date doesn't have to be well off.</span></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Absence of necessity can also be expressed by negative form of <span class=\"italic\">need</span>. It is generally used as a main verb in the construction <span class=\"italic\">don't need to</span>, but sometimes can be used as a modal, like <span class=\"italic\">needn't</span>. The infinitive after the modal verb \"needn't\" is used without the particle \"to\".  </br>Compare these sentences: </br><span class=\"italic\">You don't need to rush into a relationship right now. </br>You needn't rush into a relationship right now.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here is a list of modals of necessity:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Modal</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"necessity lack of necessity (negative)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You have to tell her. You don't have to make a reservation.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"strong necessity prohibition (negative)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We must meet after eight.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ought to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"strong advisability\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You ought to tell her that you're not into her.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"should \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"strong advisability\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You should have set this girl straight a long time ago.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You have to tell her to get lost."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It has to be on Friday night."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We must meet after eight because she has plans before then."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You don't even have to make a reservation."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should have set this girl straight a long time ago."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to blow off"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cancel without proper notice"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I blew off a meeting with my brother. I said I was too tired."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use if you make a huge mistake!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to block"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to obstruct"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I blocked the person I don't like from my social media."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "a screw loose"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a crazy person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He always says the strangest things. I think he has a screw loose."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "go dutch"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "pay for your own expenses"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When I go on a date, the girl and I always go dutch."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "take a hike"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "go away"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I told the loud salesman to take a hike."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "set straight"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "explain something clearly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I set my cousin straight about what happens in high school."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a story about a regret."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use details about the situation, what happened and personal feelings to enhance the story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use wish + past simple to help describe feelings in the story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give feedback to a partner and take feedback from a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a story about 200 words in length about something you regret doing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe in detail the situation, what happened and your feelings before and afterwards."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use wish + past simple in your story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Exchange your story with a partner and ask for feedback."}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le10ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le10ob05re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le10ob05re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: So did you blow off the meeting that woman?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I tried but she said she likes men who play hard to get. I wish I hadn't contacted her. She's been messaging me all day.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Block her! Obviously this person has a screw loose! You have to tell her to get lost.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I can't.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You realize you are just leading her on.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le10ob05re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I know. Hold on, I got a message. It's her.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Who?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: SWEET GIRL. She says dinner at the Bistro would be great, but it has to be on Friday night and we must meet after eight because she has plans before then.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Cool. You don't even have to make a reservation.  Now, I wish we had some live music for tonight.  So are you going to go Dutch?", "id": 2, "time": "21000", "image": "engenn10le10ob05re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Wait another message. It's SWEDEGURL. She says ... I can't repeat it.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Tell her you are not interested.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Ok. Ok. \u201cI wish ... that you lived close by, but you don't, sorry.\u201d\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Peter!", "id": 3, "time": "44000", "image": "engenn10le10ob05re2img05.jpg"}]}}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about relationships and personal traits."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss hopes and wishes for the present and the future. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express what is and isn't necessary."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Have you ever ha